{"auditVerdictAtHead":"pass","canonicalDigest":"sha256:d8454263cc2ae9b9992dac3e8fa6070e0f9053282191c0fc8d832a23e5612771","canonicalizationVersion":"1","changeRequest":{"author":"Bartok9","body":"## Why\n\n`omarchy transcode` (and any other `omarchy-menu-file` caller) never opens a picker when `~/Pictures` or `~/Videos` is a symlink to a real directory. GNU find does not treat symlink starting points as directories to descend into by default, so the pipeline yields 0 files and `omarchy-menu-select` gets empty stdin.\n\nPart of #12665 (discovery only; large-library selector arg-size limit is separate).\n\n## What\n\nPass `-H` to `find` so **command-line** symlink directory roots are followed without traversing interior links (avoids nested-loop/`pipefail` failures that `-L` can cause after a successful pick). Same sort (`%T@` newest first) and selector as before.\n\nAlso:\n- Expanded `-H` comment (interior symlink dirs intentionally not descended)\n- Dedup rows after `cut -f2-` with `awk '!seen[$0]++'` for overlapping roots\n- Shell regression tests for symlink root, interior loop + pipefail, broken symlink path, overlapping roots\n\n## Note\n\nReplacement for #12668 (accidentally closed during a force-push rewrite of the first commit message from `fixes #12665` → `part of #12665` so merge won't auto-close the issue while arg-size remains open). Same branch head.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `~/Videos` is a symlink to a directory with `.webm`/`.mp4`: `omarchy transcode` should open the picker.\n- Nested interior symlink loops must not turn a successful pick into exit 1.\n- Overlapping roots (e.g. Pictures → Videos) → single row per file.\n- Broken symlink path → Path not found / exit 1.\n- Direct (non-symlink) `~/Pictures`/`~/Videos` unchanged.","bodyDigest":"sha256:4bbfd510de4824f029ddb8b3a5b9783112d77074d31d72b0c25074aa74687214","bodyExcerpt":"## Why","linkedIssues":["#12665"],"source":"explicit","title":"Follow symlink dirs in omarchy-menu-file"},"createdAt":"2026-10-02T02